<title>UK: Astra researching wider Pulmicort use.</title>
<headline>Astra researching wider Pulmicort use.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish drug company Astra AB said on Monday it was researching the use of the Pulmicort Turbuhaler for chronic respiratory difficulties for smokers and the results would be published in September 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;If the Pulmicort Turbuhaler is effective on smokers, we have a market which is as big as the asthma market where there is no treatment already,&quot; head of Astra's drug division Hakan Bjorklund told a seminar.</p>
<p>The study, called Euroscop, includes 900 patients.</p>
<p>-- Lena Torlegard, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1018</p>
